  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved wage policies in KSA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The International Labour Organization (ILO) will conduct an in-depth analysis of the existing wage policies in the country, assessing how these policies are being implemented and their effectiveness in achieving fair and equitable wages. This analysis will involve identifying key challenges and obstacles that hinder the success of current wage structures, such as issues related to minimum wage enforcement, wage disparities, or labor market conditions. Based on this evaluation, the ILO will develop a series of policy recommendations that respond to different potential future scenarios, ensuring the proposed solutions are adaptable and relevant to changing economic and social conditions. These scenarios might include changes in the labour market, economic growth, inflation, or shifts in employment patterns, allowing for a comprehensive approach to improving wage policy.</narrative>
  </description>
